WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
Good morning, Hank, it's Wednesday, July 26th.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:07.260
VidCon starts tomorrow, and I have lots of exciting announcements today, beginning with the boxes behind--

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.920
What? What are you doing there?

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:09.660
[Other John]: Signing books?

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.960
[First John]: Well, get out of the frame!

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.860
[Other John}: Alright.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.920
Ugh, clones, Hank.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.640
You can't live with them, and you can't sign a crap ton of books without them.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.540
So Hank, exciting announcement number one: Penguin has moved the publication date

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.600
of The Fault in Our Stars forward by five months from

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.640
May 1st to January 10th, the book will now be published on January 10th, 2012.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.180
They called me and they were like, "We've been watching the comments on your internet television show, and

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.900
it appears that the Nerdfighters would like the book to come out before May."

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.080
And I was like, "Yeah, of course they would. And so would I!"

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.460
And then poof! It happened!

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.880
Nerdfighters, I cannot thank you enough. If it weren't for your hardcore pre-ordering, people

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.160
would have to wait until May to read this book, but because you are awesome,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.860
they get to read it five months earlier!

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.400
But Hank, then there's the small matter of having agreed to autograph every copy

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.520
of the first printing of The Fault in Our Stars; I knew that would be quite an endeavor

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.760
but um... yeah.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.780
The Yeti actually made me a thermometer...

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.180
to help me chart my progress...

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.140
all the way to 150,000 books.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.960
So Hank, we've learned to never underestimate Nerdfighters, right? I mean,

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.680
these are people who raised 150,000 dollars in 48 hours during the Project for Awesome,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.840
people who got your album on the Billboard charts,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.580
people who chartered airplanes full of life-saving medical supplies to Haiti,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:26.220
people who got Helen Hunt to hear the Helen Hunt song and threaten you with a restraining order,

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.720
and yet, it seems I have managed again to underestimate Nerdfighteria.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.340
Hank, a Nerdfighter recently guessed on her blog that I'd have to sign

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:37.640
70,000 books in about 180 days and according to her calculations, I couldn't do it.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:42.720
Well, I have to sign twice that many books in half that much time and I'm gonna do it!

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.260
I'm just not quite sure how, so I'm going to call Brotherhood 2.0 resident mathematician and

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.720
Illinois state representative Daniel Biss.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:54.100
So I have to sign 150,000, uh, copies, of The Fault in Our Stars.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.420
[Daniel]: 2,000 books a day.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.840
[John]: 2,000 books a day.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:06.620
Yeah, I mean it's not a lot of books to do in one day, it's a lot of books to do...75 days in a row.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:12.620
So Hank, these boxes contain 150,000 pages, I sign each of them and then they go to Pennsylvania,

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:16.560
where, together with the rest of the pages in the Fault in Our Stars, they are bound

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.260
and there's a cover, which I'd like to show you, but it doesn't exist yet.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.260
Although here are some awesome covers designed by nerdfighters.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.360
So I've got a couple of things working in my favour here;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.140
Number 1: My signature, like my rap name is J-Scribble,

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.800
relatively straightforward; in fact, this is the first one I signed.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.220
I should probably write a little note or something.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.700
This was the first one.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.360
Cool note, bro.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.860
And Number 2: I really want to sign all these books for you, because I like

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.980
the idea of all these signed books going into awesome, nerdfight-astic homes;

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.300
it's like if I had a ton of puppies and they all got adopted by awesome people.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.200
Long story short, all pre-orders, not matter where you live,

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:54.200
the US, the UK, Canada, Malaysia, all pre-orders of The Fault in Our Stars will be signed.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.340
I promise, I'm gonna get it done!  Links in the dooblydoo,

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.000
which is now sometimes kind of over here, if you're watching on the aggressive panda.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:06.000
And lastly, Hank, there is the question of Sharpie color; nerdfighters voted in a poll in Your Pants

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.660
about which color Sharpie I should use to sign these books. Green won.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.660
But I don't really ascribe to 'winner take all' philosophy, so I'm gonna do it like a German federal parliament,

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.660
where it's like 40 percent green, 20 percent purple, etcetera.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:22.500
Oh, and there's one more awesome announcement, next year's Vidcon will be at the Anaheim Convention Center.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:28.440
Even if you can't go to this year's Vidcon, you can go to Vidcon.com and sign up to find out more about next year.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.240
Hank, I will see you tomorrow!

